#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Guarded host-side Arch rootfs installer for the Samsung SM-X810.

It uses the shared guided preflight and confirmation flow while keeping the
Arch install narrower: it accepts rooted/unlocked Android or an
already-open TWRP session, and the sole block-device write is formatting the
existing PARTLABEL=linuxroot as ext4. Before formatting, it saves the Android
boot set to the host and seeds it into the new rootfs. It never writes GPT,
Android userdata, boot images, recovery, vbmeta, or reboots.
"""

